@template shy
// ZW1 (writer), patch 0.92.3 item 26: crew comment when you wear dirty clothes. clothes.remark: yesterday's clothes
// (flag:clothes.stale); clothes.grubby: a grubby uniform (flag:clothes.grubby, AC3). Bubbles, 60 characters or fewer.
// Kind, never mean: the joke is on the clothes, not on you.
== clothes.remark
? flag:clothes.stale
- Um. Same shirt as yesterday? It's fine. Just...
- Laundry's on Deck 4. If you, um. Need it.
? flag:clothes.stale tier>=friend
- I can show you the washers. If you want.   #warm
== clothes.grubby
? flag:clothes.grubby
- You've got... oil. There. And there.
- Oh. You're a bit... grubby. Sorry.
? flag:clothes.grubby tier>=friend
- Go and change? I'll wait. It's fine.   #warm

// ---- ZW1 (writer), patch 0.92.5 item 5: more lines for the chat card's opener (greet, near), so a tap doesn't repeat.
// Heard after a person's own lines are used up (FX13's no-repeat). {hi}, {nick} and {me} are the speaker's own words.
== greet
- Oh. Hi.
- Um. {hi}. Hello.
- Oh, it's you. That's... nice. Hi.
- {hi}. I was just... here. Hello.
- Hi. Sorry. I didn't see you there.
- {hi}. Are you... all right? Good.
- Oh. Hello. I'm a bit quiet today. Always, really.
- {hi}. I like your... never mind. Hi.
? tier>=acquaintance
- {hi}, {nick}. I'm glad it's you.
- Oh, good. It's you. I can talk to you.
? time:morning
- Morning. It's early. Isn't it?
? time:evening
- Evening. Quiet out. I like it.
== near
- I'm just... doing this. Sorry.
- {room}. It's nice in here. Quiet.
- Don't mind me. I'll be done soon.
- I'm not very good at this yet. Getting there.
- Oh. You can stay. If you want.
- Um. Hold that? Thanks.
- It's easier when nobody's watching. You're fine, though.
- Nearly done. I think.
